  "note": "From the OpenStreetMap export (tools/osm-to-kit.mjs and the corridor's tracks, 8 October 2026), 1.25 times real across the line like the tracks: island 3/4 between platform 4 (the stopper to Manchester, turning round) and platform 3, with bay 3a cut into its north end; island 1/2 beyond the fast lines, with platform 1 on its far side where the Hazel Grove line turns round, so passengers changing between the two walk through the subway; the platform 0 bay outside it; the carriage sidings and the Edgeley lines to the west; No.1 signal box on the end of island 3/4 and No.2 between the lines at the north end. Positive v is east (Station Road, Grand Central). The island buildings are set back from platform 4's edge to leave room to wait, from memory. Photos: platform 4's long canopy on slim red columns, the glass entrance with a curved roof on Station Road, a long brick retaining wall along the Station Road approach, and the Network Rail depot south of the station. It starts as a halt: a strip of island 3/4 along platform 4 with a shelter and lamps. The subway, then platform 3 (the rest of the island, and room for a second train to turn), the booking hall (the island's buildings and the Station Road building), and platforms 0, 1 and 2 build it up; the sidings, signal boxes, depot, walls and car park are scenery. Departure boards on platforms 4, 3 and 1 and over the Station Road entrance; cars on the roof deck of the multi-storey car park, and Sheffield stands by the Station Road entrance (from memory) with the booking hall.",
